# LUCI social media

Canonical strategy: **`LUCI Systems Design System/ui_kits/content-marketing/social-media-strategy.html`**. Read it before drafting any social post. This rule distills the always-follow parts so they apply automatically.

## Channel & cadence

- **LinkedIn, company page only** (Phase 1). Mike's personal page is a later phase, not now.
- **2–3 posts per week.** Consistency beats volume. If the bench is empty, post twice — never manufacture a third to hit a quota.
- Default weekly rhythm: **Mon** = weekly series · **Wed** = field or case study · **Fri** = thought leadership or news (conditional third post).

## The five post types

Every post is one of: (1) client in-the-field, (2) case study / snippet, (3) thought leadership (Mike), (4) industry / partner news, (5) the weekly series. If a draft doesn't clearly fit one, cut it or reframe it.

## Messaging discipline (the one rule the visuals fight)

- **LED walls, racks, before/after, process video = the hook, never the headline.** The caption always closes on the abstraction: one interface, one team, one accountable system.
- **Every post routes to one of the four pillars** (01 visibility/control, 02 align teams, 03 activate guest experience, 04 A/V that scales & improves). No pillar, no post.
- **Prefer diagram-led posts** when the goal is the abstraction. Canonical diagrams (What LUCI is, Consolidation ledger, System architecture, Embedded Operation orbit) are available and on-brand.
- **Write for the person running the property, not the person racking the gear.** Audience is IT and operations leadership (Dir/VP/C-suite), not A/V technicians.

## Anonymization & client rules (hard)

- **No client names on in-the-field posts.** No property-identifiable signage, uniforms, or landmarks.
- **State it's a work in progress, not a finished project.** Promise the finalized view; keep a placeholder for the reveal post.
- **Named case study or named video only with the client's OK on file.** Unnamed video is fine.
- **No timelines, scope, pricing, or go-live claims** in field posts.
- **No % boasts or unverified metrics** in brand copy (proof rules from Messaging Guide).

## Sign-off workflow (weekly batch) — nothing posts without Mike's OK

1. Jane + Cursor draft the week's 2–3 posts in the **Social Studio** (`social-studio.html`) using per-type templates.
2. Jane self-reviews: anonymization, competitor screen, voice flags. Fix or cut before Mike sees it.
3. Finalize into **`social-this-week.html`**, rebuild the review portal. The page is linked from the existing Review Queue — no new queue section.
4. Mike reviews the one page, one sitting, comments or approves the batch.
5. Jane applies comments. If Mike kills a post, it's killed — no revival. His edit wins.
6. Jane posts the approved batch to LinkedIn manually; marks each Live in the Content Lab.

**Loosening the gate:** after ~8–10 clean batches, revisit. The weekly series and approved-format snippets may move to a lighter heads-up batch. **Client-in-field and first-person Mike copy stay gated indefinitely.** Mike decides when, not us.

## News guardrails

- **Commentary, not re-share.** Add a LUCI point of view on top, or don't post.
- **No competitor promotion.** When in doubt, don't post — downside is asymmetric.
- **Partner news only when the integration is already public.** Pre-announcement = wait, no exceptions, even indirectly.
- **Honesty Protocol.** Credit partners/backends by name. Never imply LUCI owns native zone logic or routing that belongs to a third party (e.g. Q-SYS).

## Voice (short — full canon in `luci-messaging-voice.mdc` + Messaging Guide)

- **Always A/V** — never "AV" or "A-V" — in body, captions, alt text, hashtags, and on visuals.
- **Never "layer" as a noun for LUCI.** Use *orchestration engine* / *LUCI orchestrates…*.
- **Describe what the platform does, not how it feels.** "Operate every endpoint from one interface" passes; "absurdly simple" does not.
- **Watch repetition** of *engine* / *orchestrates* in a short caption — rotate to a precise alternative.
- **Institutions, not adjectives.** Declarative, subtraction framing.

## Where the work happens

- **Content Lab** (`index.html`) — input side: sources, mined ideas, voice flags.
- **Social Studio** (`social-studio.html`) — drafting workspace, one template per post type.
- **This week's posts** (`social-this-week.html`) — clean Mike-facing review page, linked from the Review Queue.
- **Transcript miner** (`scripts/mine-transcripts.mjs`) — surfaces candidate insights from past Cursor transcripts into the Content Lab.

